<!DOCTYPE document PUBLIC "-//Apache Software Foundation//DTD XDOC 1.0//EN" "http://maven.apache.org/dtd/xdoc_1_0.dtd">
<document>
  <properties>
    <title>How to use HST Spring Security Support</title>
  </properties>
  <body>

    <section name="Introduction">
      <p>
        You can install HST Spring Security Support with example configuration files by either automatically through
        Essentials or manually by editing some files in your project.
      </p>
      <p>
        The first section below will describe how to install the module with example configuration files automatically
        through Essentials, and read the following section and the <a href="configuration.html">Configuration</a> page
        if you want to install it manually.
      </p>
      <p>&nbsp;</p>
    </section>

    <section name="Installing HST Spring Security Support through Essentials">

      <subsection name="Add essentials plugin to your project">

        <p>
          In the essentials pom (<code>essentials/pom.xml</code>), add the following dependency:
        </p>

        <div class="brush: xml">
        <source><![CDATA[
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.onehippo.forge.hst-springsec</groupId>
      <artifactId>hst-springsec-essentials</artifactId>
      <version>${hst-springsec.version}</version>
    </dependency>
         ]]></source>
         </div>

        <p>&nbsp;</p>

      </subsection>

      <subsection name="Find and Install HST Spring Security Support in Essentials">
        <p>
          Now open <code>/essentials/</code> in your web browser. Find <strong>HST Spring Security Support</strong>
          plugin and install it. It will ask you to rebuild and restart the project.
          After restarting it, <strong>HST Spring Security Support</strong> is already configured.
        </p>
        <p>
          Essentials also copies all the configuration files explained in the
          <a href="configuration.html">Configuration</a> page to your project.
        </p>
        <p>&nbsp;</p>
      </subsection>

    </section>

    <section name="Installing HST Spring Security Support Manually">

      <subsection name="Add the Forge repository configuration">

        <p>In the main <code>pom.xml</code> of the project, in the <code>repositories</code> section, add this repository
          if it is not configured there yet.</p>

        <div class="brush: xml">
          <source><![CDATA[
    <repository>
      <id>bloomreach-forge</id>
      <name>Bloomreach Forge maven 2 repository.</name>
      <url>https://maven.bloomreach.com/repository/maven2-forge/</url>
    </repository>
        ]]></source>
        </div>

      </subsection>

      <subsection name="Add the version property to the project pom">

        <p>In the main <code>pom.xml</code> of the project, in the <code>properties</code> section, add this property.
          For the correct version number, check the <a href="release-notes.html">Release Notes</a> page.</p>

        <div class="brush: xml">
          <source><![CDATA[
    <hst-springsec.version>version.number</hst-springsec.version>
        ]]></source>
        </div>

        <p>Do not define <code>spring-security.version</code> yourself. It is inherited from the Bloomreach Experience Manager
          parent pom, so the Spring Security version always matches the Spring Framework version of the platform.</p>

      </subsection>

      <subsection name="Manage the dependency versions in the project pom">

        <p>In the main <code>pom.xml</code> of the project, add these to the <code>dependencyManagement</code> section.
          The Spring Framework artifacts are excluded because they are already provided by Bloomreach Experience Manager.</p>

        <div class="brush: xml">
          <source><![CDATA[
  <dependencyManagement>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-security-core</artifactId>
        <version>${spring-security.version}</version>
        <exclusions>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-aop</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-beans</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-context</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-core</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-expression</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
        </exclusions>
      </dependency>

      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-security-web</artifactId>
        <version>${spring-security.version}</version>
        <exclusions>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-beans</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-context</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-core</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-expression</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-web</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
        </exclusions>
      </dependency>

      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-security-config</artifactId>
        <version>${spring-security.version}</version>
        <exclusions>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-aop</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-beans</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-context</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
          <exclusion>
            <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-core</artifactId>
          </exclusion>
        </exclusions>
      </dependency>

      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.onehippo.forge.hst-springsec</groupId>
        <artifactId>hst-springsec</artifactId>
        <version>${hst-springsec.version}</version>
      </dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </dependencyManagement>
        ]]></source>
        </div>

      </subsection>

      <subsection name="Add the dependencies to the site components">

        <p>Add these to the <code>pom.xml</code> of the <code>site/components</code> module. The versions and exclusions
          are inherited from the <code>dependencyManagement</code> section of the project pom.</p>

        <div class="brush: xml">
          <source><![CDATA[
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-security-core</artifactId>
      <scope>runtime</scope>
    </dependency>

    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-security-web</artifactId>
      <scope>runtime</scope>
    </dependency>

    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
      <artifactId>spring-security-config</artifactId>
      <scope>runtime</scope>
    </dependency>

    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.onehippo.forge.hst-springsec</groupId>
      <artifactId>hst-springsec</artifactId>
      <scope>runtime</scope>
    </dependency>
        ]]></source>
        </div>

      </subsection>

      <subsection name="Add the configuration files">

        <p>Finally, add the Spring Security configuration files described on the <a href="configuration.html">Configuration</a>
          page. The <code>SpringSecurityValve</code> configuration is a Spring XML file in the HST assembly overrides folder
          of the site components, for example
          <code>site/components/src/main/resources/META-INF/hst-assembly/overrides/spring-security.xml</code>.</p>

      </subsection>

    </section>

  </body>

</document>
